sentry-native provides CMake targets:

    find_package(sentry CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE sentry::sentry)

The backend feature enables the Native crash backend by default. Without that
feature, crash capture is disabled (SENTRY_BACKEND=none).

To select another backend, add this to a custom triplet:

    if(PORT STREQUAL "sentry-native")
        set(SENTRY_BACKEND crashpad)
    endif()

The optional wer feature only enables WER integration for an explicitly selected
Crashpad backend. Native builds and packages its own Windows WER module without
requiring that feature.

Crash helpers are installed in tools/sentry-native. Ship the selected helper
(sentry-crash or crashpad_handler) and its runtime dependencies with the
application, and configure sentry_options_set_handler_path accordingly.
The Native helper's adjacent sentry-wer.dll is required on Windows for fast-fail
crashes. Normal app-local DLL dependency scanning cannot deploy these helpers.
